'' 'operator []' called in the shape it declares: the index coerced to the operator's
'' own parameter type, and the result taken byref or byval as declared. See the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/index-operator-shape.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' THE INDEX IS NOT TRUNCATED: an 'integer' parameter is i64 here, and the argument
'' reaches it as one.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i64 _ZN3VALixEu7INTEGER(@v, %
'' EXPECT-NOT: call ptr _ZN3VALixEu7INTEGER
'' ...and the BYREF operator keeps the pointer shape, because that is what makes
'' 'r[ 2 ] = 99' an lvalue.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call ptr _ZN3REFixEu7INTEGER(@r, %
'' GOLDEN: expected/index-operator-shape.out
